            <ArticleTitle>[Chronic intestinal ischaemia in a younger patient].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1907-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 46-year-old woman presented with classic symptoms. Computed tomography-angiography and duplex ultrasonography showed stenosis of the aa. mesenteria superior et inferior. The patient was moved to a university hospital and a percutaneous transluminal angioplasty with insertion of stents was performed. She was discharged shortly after feeling well.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
